What is Ciprofloxacin Lactate for Injection?
Ciprofloxacin Lactate for Injection is a broad-spectrum antibiotic formulation that combines ciprofloxacin's bactericidal properties with enhanced solubility through lactate conjugation. As a fluoroquinolone antibiotic, it inhibits bacterial DNA gyrase and topoisomerase IV enzymes, effectively disrupting DNA replication in both Gram-negative and some Gram-positive pathogens. The lactate formulation provides critical advantages for intravenous administration, including improved bioavailability and reduced injection site irritation compared to standard preparations.
